# Compiled binaries.
#
# `go build` inside an example writes an executable named after its module —
# examples/prisma/prisma, examples/socket.io/socketio, and so on. Together those
# were 33MB of the 34MB staged here.
#
# The rule below ignores every extensionless path one level down, because every
# source file an example tracks has an extension (.go, .mod, .sum, .md, .json,
# .html, .txt). The `!/*/*/` line keeps directories traversable so subdirectories
# are still considered. If an example ever needs an extensionless file of its own
# — a Makefile, say — negate it explicitly.
/*/*
!/*/*.*
!/*/*/

# Output the examples generate when run. They are reproducible with `go run .`,
# so committing them would only create diff noise.
*/out/
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
